## 2. PROJECT CONCEPT

The user scans a specially designed automobile advertisement printed in a newspaper or magazine.

The web application opens on their smartphone.

The smartphone camera recognises the printed advertisement using image-target tracking.

A realistic 3D automobile model appears anchored to the advertisement.

The user can:
- View the complete automobile in 3D.
- Rotate the automobile.
- Zoom in and out.
- Explore different parts of the automobile.
- Tap interactive hotspots.
- Open information cards for individual components.
- View automobile specifications and materials.
- Switch between different exploration modes.

The experience must work through a mobile browser without requiring users to install a native application.

